commit f2b59667f3128ee7d080099456e631a76aa9c5e0
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 22:56:50 2026 +0000

    scanner: sqlmap's DBMS error bank and boolean SQLi detection on dynamic pages

    Error bank (v0ei.2). sqlmap's data/xml/errors.xml (187 regexes, 31
    engines) is embedded verbatim with sqlmap's LICENSE and an attribution
    README under internal/scanner/sqlmapdata (GPLv2-or-later; burpsy is
    GPL-3.0-or-later). Reused from 04a546d4, with the file re-fetched and
    byte-identical. It is a second bank behind Burp's substrings, under the
    same rules: a pattern counts only when the baseline did not match it, it
    is read in the received and HTML-unescaped forms, and a pattern whose
    every match starts on a shell's own diagnostic line is attributed to the
    shell (the j1mk.40 rule, applied per match position). Matches name their
    engine; the probe detail says "the error identifies the DBMS as X". The
    online probe, ClassifySQLError and the no-sender read all use it.

